                <pb facs="0624" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.77/3654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-29T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 29—10:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>American, British, French and Japanese consular seals removed from cabinets in
                    the land department Chinese Eastern Railway this afternoon on the initiative of
                    the four consuls. Informed the Embassy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
